  "note": "Greek spells names by sound. Greek has no single b, d or g letter for those sounds, so they're written μπ, ντ, γκ; 'j' is τζ. Put the accent (á é í ó) on the stressed vowel, use ς for an 's' at the very end, and capitalize the first letter.",
